            0.08
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fractions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.118,
            0.616,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 1. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{5}{8} - \\frac{3}{8}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 2. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{7}{9} - \\frac{5}{9}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 3. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 0 } { 2 7 } - \\frac { 1 } { 2 7 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.204,
            0.834,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Subtraction of fractions with different fractional units or denominators",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.253,
            0.382,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ": What is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 4 } - \\frac { 2 } { 3 } ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.286,
            0.836,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As we already know the procedure for subtraction of fractions with the same fractional units, let us convert each of the given fractions into equivalent fractions with the same fractional units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.423,
            0.39,
            0.688,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Yes! By doing this we can easily subtract the two fractions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.369,
            0.816,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.127,
                0.369,
                0.816,
                0.693
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_30_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.422,
            0.473,
            0.702,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think! Why did we choose to multiply both the numerator and denominator by 3?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.455,
            0.589,
            0.777,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Again! Why did we choose to multiply both the numerator and denominator here by 4?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.661,
            0.443,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{9}{12} - \\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{1}{12}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.703,
            0.737,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Brahmagupta’s method for subtracting two fractions —",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.732,
            0.833,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Convert the given fractions into equivalent fractions with the same fractional unit, i.e., the same denominator."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.782,
            0.834,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Carry out the subtraction of fractions having the same fractional units. This can be done by subtracting the numerators and keeping the same denominator."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.853,
            0.656,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Simplify the result into lowest terms if needed."
            }
          ]
        },
